                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "27212b55-9c61-4b0f-b11c-72f312b48891",
                        "source_entry_id": "99b7399f-b741-3969-8456-59c4848131a9",
                        "source_sense_id": "d0cea5b0-76ce-3751-8e64-c32a4778f63a",
                        "target_lang_word": "nocebo",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nocebo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "baf52ed8-af22-3143-995e-fb76b525d83f",
                                        "entry_id": "9950485e-2905-3278-89b5-bd8360b0533a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substance which a patient experiences as harmful due to a previous negative perception, but which is in fact pharmacologically (medicinally) inactive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "attributive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a178ce13-6c4e-4dcf-8eb9-5f96cb10e7e5",
                                                "sense_id": "baf52ed8-af22-3143-995e-fb76b525d83f",
                                                "text": "In the case of the nocebo, it is negative expectations that become self-fulfilling prophecies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "038f1453-e15c-4d50-ae93-6250a27120ae",
                                                "sense_id": "baf52ed8-af22-3143-995e-fb76b525d83f",
                                                "text": "It is somewhat surprising that little attention has been drawn to the existence of the contrary effect [to the placebo] – which I may call the nocebo reaction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83273584-a7c9-4373-9aac-5c678c4dea09",
                                                "sense_id": "baf52ed8-af22-3143-995e-fb76b525d83f",
                                                "text": "It seems to be a \"nocebo\" effect – the self-diagnosed gluten sensitive patients expected to feel worse on the study diets, so they did."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9951f0b-ce8f-46f2-b089-582097ce2898",
                                                "sense_id": "baf52ed8-af22-3143-995e-fb76b525d83f",
                                                "text": "If there's one lesson to be drawn from the nocebo effect, it's that ideas are never merely ideas. […] Maybe you see where I'm going with this: our grim view of humanity is also a nocebo."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
